  "review_notes": [
    "*Forty years old was I* is a verbless age clause: בֶּן carries *old* together with the copula, and אָנֹכִי keeps only *I* (rule 20).",
    "The *it* of *as it was in my heart* is assigned to דָּבָר as rule 25's resumed referent; the alternative is an `added` impersonal subject, and that reading is named in the unit's note."
